#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.65pt, 789.816pt, "1 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 86.76pt, "Direction-dependent photo-voltage detection in multifunctional ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 114.38pt, "ZnO micro rod/PBTTT-C14 polymer sensor due to gold ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 141.98pt, "nanoparticles ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(211.73pt, 189.74pt, "Rehan Ahmed and Pramod Kumar* ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 216.38pt, "Department of Physics, Indian Institute of Technology Bombay, Mumbai 400076, India ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 243.14pt, "*Author to whom any correspondence should be addressed ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 273.86pt, "*Email Address: pramod_k@iitb.ac.in  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 304.85pt, "Abstract  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 325.25pt, "A sensor that can detect the direction of the incoming light plays a crucial role in further ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 346.01pt, "enhancing the versatility of the multifunction sensors for future applications where the sensor ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 366.65pt, "can read multiple pieces of information, similar to the biological senses, like skin. A hybrid ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 387.29pt, "sensor based on an n-type ZnO micro-rod with p-type optically active organic polymer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 408.05pt, "(PBTTT-C14) is developed for low-cost, large-area piezoelectric and optical sensing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 428.69pt, "applications for future artificial electronic skin. The multi-functionality of the device is ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 449.45pt, "achieved due to the heterostructure configuration of vertically aligned piezoelectric ZnO micro ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 470.11pt, "rod arrays and PBTTT-C14 polymer between two gold electrodes. The deposition of the top ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 490.87pt, "gold electrode also led to the formation of two regions where it forms a continuous film and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 511.51pt, "isolated gold particles (Au NPs). The isolated NPs when activated, has shown surface plasmon ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 532.27pt, "resonance (SPR) and Förster resonance energy transfer (FRET) which generate a potential ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 552.91pt, "opposite to the normal working of the device, depending on the number of excited Au NPs by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 573.67pt, "the incident light. The polarity flipping/opposite potential development can be attributed to the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 594.31pt, "rise in electron density near top Au contact due to the SPR and FRET mechanism of isolated ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 615.07pt, "Au NPs over the PBTTT-C14 which depends on the illumination direction. As a result, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 635.71pt, "direction-dependent photo voltage polarity flipping was realized in the device. The device has ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 656.5pt, "produced piezoelectric and direction-dependent photovoltage flipping responses, leading the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 677.14pt, "way for a multifunction sensor that can detect the direction of incident light and touch. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 718.54pt, "Keywords: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(130.94pt, 718.54pt, "Hybrid piezoelectric-optoelectronic sensor, organic semiconductors (PBTTT-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 739.3pt, "C14), piezoelectricity, SPR and FRET, voltage polarity flipping. ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.65pt, 789.816pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 83.16pt, "1.")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 83.16pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.58pt, "In recent years, advancements in the field of machine learning and robotics have required the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 124.34pt, "development of sensors and devices that can mimic biological senses like touch, smell, vision, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 144.98pt, "hearing, and brain function [1], [2], [3], [4]. The biological sense, like skin, can not only detect ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.74pt, "touch but also temperature changes; it has multiple other functions like regulating the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 186.38pt, "temperature by sweating, acting as a barrier against harmful substances and pathogens, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 207.14pt, "production of vitamin D, and storage of fat and other nutrients [5], [6]. Taking a cue from the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 227.78pt, "biological senses, it is also logical to fabricate sensors and devices which can perform multiple ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 248.54pt, "functions [7], [8]. Inorganic and organic semiconductors have shown photo-detection ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 269.18pt, "capability, which can be enhanced by using heterojunctions, including inorganic/organic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 289.97pt, "heterojunctions [9]. Organic semiconductors are carbon-based molecules or polymers and have ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 310.61pt, "received a great deal of interest due to their advantages, including solution processing, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 331.37pt, "mechanical flexibility, lightweight nature, low-cost production, and tunable bandgaps [9]. The ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 352.01pt, "photo sensors based on the organic semiconductors that harvest the light signals into electrical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 372.77pt, "signals have a wide range of applications in optical communication, health monitoring, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 393.41pt, "image sensors [10], [11], [12]. The organic materials can be easily processed into the device ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 414.17pt, "structure by spin coating and inkjet printing techniques [13]. They are capable of detecting the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 434.81pt, "ultraviolet (UV), visible, and near-infrared (NIR) wavelengths, depending on the bandgap of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 455.57pt, "the material. Inorganic semiconductor-based devices/photodetectors are generally made from ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 476.23pt, "materials like silicon (Si) and gallium arsenide (GaAs) which have been extensively used [14], ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 496.99pt, "[15]. However, the inorganic thin film devices are relatively difficult and costly to fabricate on ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 517.63pt, "flexible substrates and therefore difficult to use in flexible electronic applications, as they have ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 538.39pt, "high brittleness and complicated manufacturing process. The majority of inorganic photoactive ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 559.03pt, "materials exhibit a fixed light absorption with narrow spectral sensitivity, resulting in the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 579.79pt, "detection of only specific wavelengths within a narrow band [16]. The traditional inorganic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 600.43pt, "materials-based devices due to the above reasons are unsuitable for low-cost flexible ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 621.19pt, "photodetectors. Hence, new materials and device heterostructure are needed for enhancement ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 641.83pt, "of the device sensitivity and capability. Therefore, the combination of hybrid organic-inorganic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 662.62pt, "heterostructure (O-I HJ) may be considered as excellent device structure for making it highly ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 683.26pt, "efficient and more capable. The O-I HJ provides the benefits of both organic and inorganic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 704.02pt, "materials and gives a broader platform for applications in multifunction devices. Several p-type ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 724.66pt, "organic semiconductors and n-type inorganic semiconductors from group III-V or II-VI offer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 745.416pt, "an excellent platform for creating p-n junctions [12]. There are several useful inorganic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 766.056pt, "semiconductors such as ZnO and GaN. Interfaces involving inorganic semiconductors with π-")
]

// arXiv source page 3
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.65pt, 789.816pt, "3 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.92pt, "conjugated organic semiconductors (polymers) can be utilized for hybrid junctions [17], [18], ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.58pt, "[19]. The ZnO has advantages over other inorganic semiconductors because of its non-toxic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 124.34pt, "nature and biocompatibility, and it can also be easily synthesized with a low-cost hydrothermal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 144.98pt, "method at low temperatures [20], [21], [22]. Due to its distinct physical properties, including ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.74pt, "mechanical flexibility and high sensitivity, the ZnO based hybrid organic-inorganic interfaces ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 186.38pt, "have attracted significant attention [19]. Various photoactive organic materials such as PBTTT-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 207.14pt, "C14 Poly[2,2'-(1,4-phenylene)-6,6'-bis(4-phenylquinoline)], P3HT (poly(3-hexylthiophene)), ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 227.78pt, "PTCDI ")
  #line-at(127.668pt, 227.78pt, "(Perylenetetracarboxylic ")
  #line-at(266.544pt, 227.78pt, "diimide), ")
  #line-at(331.416pt, 227.78pt, "and ")
  #line-at(369.804pt, 227.78pt, "PEDOT:PSS ")
  #line-at(452.916pt, 227.78pt, "(Poly ")
  #line-at(499.932pt, 227.78pt, "(3,4-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 248.54pt, "ethylenedioxythiophene) polystyrene sulfonate) are commonly integrated with the inorganic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 269.18pt, "materials in hybrid photodetector fabrications [23], [24], [25], [26]. Among these materials, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 289.97pt, "PBTTT-C14 is well known for its high charge carrier mobility and stability [27]. PBTTT-C14 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 310.61pt, "exhibits a strong absorption in the UV and visible range, and this absorption profile makes it a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 331.37pt, "suitable and promising candidate for light-harvesting applications in organic photovoltaics ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 352.01pt, "[25]. PBTTT-C14 is frequently used as an electron donor (p-type semiconducting material) in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 372.77pt, "organic-inorganic photovoltaic applications. These properties of PBTTT-C14 make it suitable ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 393.41pt, "for applications in organic electronics [28]. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 414.17pt, "In this research work, we have demonstrated an integration of hydrothermally grown ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 434.81pt, "piezoelectric/semiconductor ZnO micro rods with organic semiconductor PBTTT-C14 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 455.57pt, "polymer. The hybrid ZnO/PBTTT-C14 heterostructure provides both piezoelectric and optical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 476.23pt, "stimulus response, and the directionality of the optical signal is detected with a third ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 496.99pt, "component, which is the Au NPs. The electrical signals collected from the multifunction Au ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 517.63pt, "NPs/PBTTT-C14/ZnO based hybrid device can have potential applications in piezo-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 538.39pt, "optoelectronics and artificial skin sensors for robotics. The multifunctionality is achieved due ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 559.03pt, "to the piezoelectric, charge extraction, and optical transmission nature of ZnO micro rod arrays ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 579.79pt, "when it is introduced with an optically active polymer (PBTTT-C14). This heterostructure of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 600.43pt, "ZnO micro rods and PBTTT-C14 is realized for optical and piezoelectric responses without ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 621.19pt, "any external voltage, which means that it is a self-powered multifunctional sensor. The ZnO ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 641.83pt, "micro rod generates the piezoelectric response and helps in the hybrid charge transfer exciton ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 662.62pt, "formation and charge extraction at OI-HJ. The heterostructure of different materials has ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 683.26pt, "previously been used for the polarity flipping of the photovoltage for detecting the wavelength ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 704.02pt, "of incident light. M. Patel et.al. has shown the polarity flipping of the photovoltage using the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 724.66pt, "p-SnS/p-Si isotype heterojunction for wavelength-selective photodetectors, that exhibit ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 745.416pt, "selective photodetection and can detect the UV, visible, and near-infrared (NIR) lights by the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 766.056pt, "polarity of the generated voltage [29]. Similar results corresponding to the particular ")
]

