#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.65pt, 789.816pt, "4 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.92pt, "wavelength-selective detectors with different material heterojunctions are also been realized ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.58pt, "[30], [31], [32]. Therefore, understanding the charge extraction and energy transfer mechanism ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 124.34pt, "in Au NPs/PBTTT-C14/ZnO heterojunction is essential for constructing and describing the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 144.98pt, "device’s working mechanism. Surface Plasmon Resonance (SPR) and Fluorescence Resonance ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.74pt, "Energy Transfer (FRET) have been widely used to study the energy and electron transfer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 186.38pt, "between the ZnO, organic materials, and Au NPs [33], [34], [35], [36]. SPR is an optical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 207.14pt, "phenomenon arising from the collective oscillation of the free conduction electrons on the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 227.78pt, "noble metal nanoparticle’s surface when it is excited by photons. Au NPs decorated ZnO ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 248.54pt, "surface impacts the system in inducing the accumulation of free electrons and facilitates their ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 269.18pt, "transfer across the interface. Recent studies in photoactive organic materials have demonstrated ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 289.97pt, "that the FRET mechanism is an effective approach for improving long distance (~1-10 nm) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 310.61pt, "exciton migration [33]. FRET is a non-radiative energy transfer mechanism in which the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 331.37pt, "excitation photon is first absorbed by the donor molecules, and then the energy of the emission ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 352.01pt, "of donors is transferred to the acceptors by the interaction of the electric dipoles [37]. In the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 372.77pt, "present work, the competition between the normal operation, which is without much influence ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 393.41pt, "of the Au NPs, and with a large influence of Au NPs on the device has been identified as a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 414.17pt, "possible reason for the voltage shift due to the direction of incident light. Further, the study ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 434.81pt, "also explores the fluorescence quenching, accumulation of free electrons, and its effect on the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 455.57pt, "direction of electron transport across the interface of Au NPs/PBTTT-C14/ZnO heterojunction. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 476.23pt, "We have shown that the Au NPs/PBTTT-C14/ZnO heterojunction device can detect the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 496.99pt, "directional dependent photovoltage polarity flipping, unlike the previous research where the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 517.63pt, "device is based on wavelength selectivity. This multifunction sensor can be useful for artificial ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 538.39pt, "skin in robotics and also for orientation calibration of solar cells to achieve the highest ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 559.03pt, "efficiency. ")
