  #line-at(294.65pt, 789.816pt, "6 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.92pt, "Device without PBTTT-C14 coating is also prepared with the same fabrication procedure to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.58pt, "compare the effect of organic semiconductors. Finally, the whole device structure is packaged ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 124.34pt, "with PDMS (polydimethylsiloxane) to provide mechanical support and protect it from moisture ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 144.98pt, "and dust after making contacts on the top and bottom electrodes.  The schematic architecture ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.74pt, "of the device is presented in Figure 2, in which the large view of the single ZnO micro rod ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 186.38pt, "shows the light penetration into the PBTTT-C14 layer through the ZnO micro rod, where the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 207.14pt, "gold film is non-continuous.")
  #line-at(210.77pt, 207.14pt, "The uncoated surface of the micro rod allows the incident photon ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 227.78pt, "to enter into the PBTTT-C14 layer, and the process of photon absorption and charge extraction ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 395.81pt, "in an Au NPs-O-I heterojunction takes place. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 422.57pt, "Figure 2.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.58pt, 422.57pt, " Schematic design of the hybrid device structure, (a) represents the growth of ZnO ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 438.41pt, "NR arrays and (b) spin coating of PBTTT-C14 and then Au thin film deposition which resulted ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 454.25pt, "in the formation of Au NPs. The enlarged figure shows the light penetration through the single ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 470.11pt, "ZnO micro rod into the PBTTT-C14 layer. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 498.31pt, "2.3. Characterization techniques ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 530.71pt, "Morphological analysis of the grown ZnO micro rod was conducted with a Field Emission ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 551.35pt, "Scanning Electron Microscope (FE-SEM, JSM-7600F). The photoluminescence (PL) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 572.11pt, "measurement was done through the designed setup which consists of the He-Cd laser as the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 592.75pt, "excitation source of wavelength (λ) 325 nm. The source had an energy of 3.81 eV, which is ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 613.51pt, "sufficient to excite the electron in the ZnO semiconductor. PerkinElmer Lambda 950 UV-vis ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 634.15pt, "spectrophotometer was used for the absorption measurement. The optical measurement of the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 654.94pt, "sensor was characterized by a solar simulator (ORIEL, LSH-7320 ABA LED Solar Simulator) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 675.58pt, "and a semiconductor characterization system (Keithley 4200-SCS). The intensity of the solar ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 696.34pt, "simulator was 100 mW/cm")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(202.97pt, 691.78pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(207.05pt, 696.34pt, " and is equal to one sun. A weight-adjustable tapping mechanism ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 716.98pt, "setup is used to apply force on the device, and the generated piezoelectric voltage is measured ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 737.74pt, "with the help of a digital oscilloscope (Tektronix MDO4054-3). ")
]

