  #line-at(72.024pt, 239.78pt, "some portions of the PBTTT-C14 coated ZnO micro rods.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 439.61pt, "Figure 3.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.1pt, 439.61pt, " SEM images of Au deposited PBTTT-C14-coated ZnO micro rod, (a) top view and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 455.57pt, "the inset shows the high magnification top view image (b) cross-sectional view.")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 481.39pt, "PL and absorption measurements were carried out to investigate the changes in optical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 502.15pt, "properties of PBTTT-C14 thin films and when it was coated on ZnO micro rods based hybrid ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 522.79pt, "devices. The PBTTT-C14 was spin coated on a transparent glass slide and an optical scan from ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 543.55pt, "400 to 800 nm was carried out to determine its absorption spectrum. PBTTT-C14 polymer film ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 564.19pt, "exhibits strong absorption in the visible range, with absorption maxima at ~ 546 nm, as shown ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 584.95pt, "in Figure 4 (a). The observed spectrum shows a broad absorption band between the range ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 605.59pt, "480─650 nm, and the absorption peak is equivalent to 2.27 eV, which is in good agreement ")
