  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 368.33pt, "Figure 8.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(117.98pt, 368.33pt, " Schematic energy band diagram of Au/ZnO/Au device with Au NPs elucidating the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 384.17pt, "process of surface plasmon coupling between Au NPs and ZnO micro rods. Where the C.B., ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 400.01pt, "V.B., and D* represent the conduction band, valence band, and defect level in the ZnO, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 415.85pt, "respectively. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 441.77pt, "The polarity flipping in the Au NPs/PBTTT-C14/ZnO micro rods device, as shown in the result ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 462.41pt, "of Figure 7 (b), can be understood by the band level diagram of Figure 9. FRET is a process ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 483.19pt, "that can shed light on the charge carrier dynamics over a distance between two different ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 503.83pt, "molecules [33], [51], [52]. It is a non-radiative energy transfer mechanism by which the energy ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 524.59pt, "(emitted photon) is transferred from one molecule to an excited state to another molecule. In ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 545.23pt, "Figure 5 (b), the quenching phenomenon observed in the Au NPs/PBTTT-C14 may result from ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 565.99pt, "the interplay between the FRET and SPR effects [49]. The PBTTT-C14 device can work in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 586.63pt, "two modes, one where the density of active Au NPs is negligible which can be called normal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 607.39pt, "device operation and the second where the density of active Au NPs is very large due to the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 628.03pt, "incident light which can be described as active mode. These two competing processes can give ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 648.79pt, "rise to a photovoltage polarity flipping phenomenon. The normal mode of device operation is ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 669.46pt, "shown in Figure 9 (a) where it is assumed that the density of Au NPs is very less. In this case, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 690.22pt, "PBTTT-C14 absorbs energy and forms excitons which get separated into electron and hole and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 710.86pt, "the energy levels decide the charge carrier flow direction. The electron is collected by the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 731.62pt, "bottom Au electrode and hole by the top Au electrode. The active mode of operation is shown ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 752.256pt, "by Figure 9 (b) where the incident light falls on large number of Au NPs. Here SPR and FRET ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.447pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
