  #line-at(291.65pt, 789.816pt, "15 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.92pt, "while press and release could be attributed to the back-and-forth flow of the electrons in the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.58pt, "circuit driven by the piezoelectric potential [53]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 283.37pt, "Figure 10.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(126.02pt, 283.37pt, " The piezoelectric output result of the device while pressing and releasing the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 304.01pt, "pressure. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 332.81pt, "4.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.024pt, 332.81pt, "Conclusion")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 360.89pt, "Introducing the organic semiconductor (PBTTT-C14) into the ZnO micro rod matrix has shown ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 381.53pt, "a photovoltage polarity flipping effect, where the generated photovoltage is shifted from ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 402.29pt, "positive to negative values under different illumination directions.  The photovoltage polarity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 422.93pt, "flipping can be explained by the number of active Au NPs, which reverses the flow of the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 443.69pt, "charge carriers. When a large number of Au NPs get active due to a certain direction/angle of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 464.33pt, "incident light, both FRET and SPR take place, which results in the accumulation of electrons ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 485.11pt, "in the vicinity of the top Au electrode, resulting in photovoltage polarity flipping. The normal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 505.75pt, "mode of device operation takes place at a direction/angle where the Au NPs are relatively less ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 526.51pt, "active and electrons are guided by the band levels of PBTTT-C14 and ZnO toward the bottom ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 547.15pt, "Au electrode. Hence, the competition between the normal mode working and active mode when ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 567.91pt, "SPR and FRET mechanisms of Au NP and PBTTT-C14 are active leads to the development of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 588.55pt, "a light directional detection sensor. The proposed device can also produce approximately ~10 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 609.31pt, "mV piezoelectric signal, making it suitable for multifunctional sensing applications.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 658.78pt, "Acknowledgment")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 680.86pt, "The authors would like to thank the Indian Institute of Technology Bombay for the seed grant ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 701.5pt, "and the Science and Engineering Research Board (SERB), Government of India for funding. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 722.26pt, "R. Ahmed would like to also thank the Council of Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR), ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 742.896pt, "Government of India for providing the fellowship. The authors would also like to thank ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 763.656pt, "Amandeep Kaur and Phalguna Srinivasan for their help in PL and optical measurements. ")
]

